<!--Post: 6980--><!--Time: 1108105985-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6980"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ciajoe<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ciajoe<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 11:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After doing a google search for &#34;Bill Thomas&#34; and Xerox &#40;copiers&#41;, I found this:  <BR> <BR>&#40;See Bill Thomas bio&#41; <BR><a href="http://webs.wichita.edu/ielc/facultybio-IE.html" target=_top>http://webs.wichita.edu/ielc/facultybio-IE.html</a> <BR> <BR>I have come to the conclusion that in some way shape or form that somewhere in recent communications he sends to KAKE &#40;recently&#41; falls back to the letter with all of his claims.. age, profession, etc.  <BR> <BR>Childhood friend, Petra: WSU Brick <BR> <BR>Childhood friend, Tina: perhaps a.k.a. Christine, Petra&#39;s sister <BR><a href="http://plaza.wichita.edu/heroines/Heroine/biodisplay.asp?ID=755" target=_top>http://plaza.wichita.edu/heroines/Heroine/biodispl ay.asp?ID=755</a> <BR> <BR>Bill Thomas Killmann: Bill Thomas, Xerox teacher - falls back to the copier repair statement <BR><a href="http://webs.wichita.edu/ielc/facultybio-IE.html" target=_top>http://webs.wichita.edu/ielc/facultybio-IE.html</a> <BR> <BR>I am looking for other similarities.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6980-->
<!--Post: 6981--><!--Time: 1108106336-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6981"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ciajoe<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ciajoe<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 11:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I should also mention that.. <BR>I am not saying this is him, but I am under the impression that he is always trying to make the trail point to someone else.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6981-->
<!--Post: 6986--><!--Time: 1108108530-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6986"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 11:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Looks like a lead . Tom may delete it, though, since you used the name . You might want to post it again under &#34;THEORIES&#34;&#34;POSSIBLE SUSPECTS&#34; using only the link and no name mentioned.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6986-->
<!--Post: 6987--><!--Time: 1108108778-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6987"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 11:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correction &#34;BTK Suspects&#34; is a main thread ... not under &#34;THEORIES&#34;. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6987-->
<!--Post: 6989--><!--Time: 1108109263-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6989"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ciajoe<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ciajoe<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 12:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Like I said, I don&#39;t think this is a possible suspect, so it wouldnt be fair to post it there.  <BR> <BR>The only name I used was one that was on a postcard or letter, and the name of a person working at a public facilty.  <BR> <BR>Bill Thomas Killman on the return sender <BR> <BR>and  <BR> <BR>Bill Thomas that I think BTK was referencing on the return sender <BR> <BR>Once again, I am not saying this is a suspect.  <BR> <BR>If I violated any rule, I apologize in advance. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6989-->
<!--Post: 6991--><!--Time: 1108110725-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6991"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 12:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Theres nothing wrong with suspecting. It&#39;s just that By posting a name there is the possibility of a lawsuit. Posting a link to something on another web site is just saying &#34;this info is out there&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6991-->
<!--Post: 7007--><!--Time: 1108130294-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7007"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 5:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the lady at the top could make a better suspect candidate. She looks rather husky, and has a gap between her teeth - one of the descriptions of BTK by one of the witnesses.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7007-->
<!--Post: 7076--><!--Time: 1108172513-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7076"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 5:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, the age is right.  The time that he was in Wichita seems to coincide with the &#34;break&#34; in suspected BTK activity.  One witness described BTK as &#34;dark complected, and with a moustache.  Knowledge of photocopiers, BTK claimed to have been a copy machine repairman.  This guy has a Master&#39;s degree in Linguistics, BTK loves word games and playing with grammar/syntax, writing poetry...  He could possibly be a POI, although we just have a few superficial facts about him that could be coincidental.  <BR> <BR>I wonder if LE has ever come up with a formula to figure out how many coincidences add up to a likely perp?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7076-->
<!--Post: 7077--><!--Time: 1108172630-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7077"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 5:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another thought just occurred to me:  Could BTK be setting this guy up, using the information BTK sent to WPD claiming it was all true autobiographical info?  Like some of us think may have happened to the suspect who was arrested and swabbed in a huge media circus in December?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7077-->
<!--Post: 7094--><!--Time: 1108178688-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7094"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 7:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve only glanced at all this and will read further. I wanted to mention now that &#34;Bill Thomas&#34; or &#34;William Thomas&#34; is a very, very common name. Not saying there&#39;s not anything here, I think there may be. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7094-->
<!--Post: 7104--><!--Time: 1108183081-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7104"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 8:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m with George. BTK has made references to the university before and he is familiar with the staff. Using Mr. Thomas&#39; name is just another one of his games.  <BR> <BR>I CERTAINTLY wouldn&#39;t believe that BTK would write his real name on the card.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7104-->
<!--Post: 7298--><!--Time: 1108378975-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7298"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 3:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.petrafoundation.org/fellows/Tina_Johnstone/" target=_top>http://www.petrafoundation.org/fellows/Tina_Johnst one/</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7298-->
<!--Post: 7304--><!--Time: 1108387126-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7304"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 5:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bill Thomas Killman, someone pointed out that the word   &#34;mask&#34; is in this name. Either Davis or Hedge was found with a ceramic mardi gras type mask either on them or next to them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7304-->
